REQUEST  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/v1/employees/8d064ba1-5b12-49e7-9c05-ac21c66e5484/emergency-contacts  Authorization: Bearer <superadmin>
{"contact_name":"X","relationship":"Brother","contact_phone":"9876500001","is_primary":false,"display_order":3}
RESPONSE 409 {"detail": "Only one contact may be marked Primary"}   <- is_primary is false; the real failure is ck_eec_relationship

REQUEST  POST (same path) {"contact_name":"Y","relationship":"OTHER","contact_phone":"12345","is_primary":false,"display_order":4}
RESPONSE 409 {"detail": "Only one contact may be marked Primary"}   <- real failure is ck_eec_phone

PROOF THE STATED RULE IS NOT WHAT FIRED â€” same body with a legal relationship succeeds:
POST (same path) {"contact_name":"Raj Tester","relationship":"SIBLING","contact_phone":"9876500000","is_primary":false,"display_order":2}
-> 201 {"contact_name":"Raj Tester","relationship":"SIBLING","contact_phone":"9876500000","is_primary":false,"display_order":2,"id":"22496653-af8e-45d1-8c00-5645fd8c30ba", ...}

SCHEMA: SHOW CREATE TABLE employee_emergency_contacts -> CONSTRAINT `ck_eec_relationship` CHECK ((`relationship` is null) or (`relationship` in ('SPOUSE','PARENT','SIBLING','FRIEND','OTHER'))), CONSTRAINT `ck_eec_phone` CHECK ((`contact_phone` is null) or regexp_like(`contact_phone`,'^[6-9][0-9]{9}$'))
OpenAPI EmergencyContactWrite -> "relationship": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}]}  (no enum)

Setup (200): POST /api/v1/employees/32f38afa-06a7-4d6e-b56b-a5370654cffb/tax-scheme-elections {"tax_scheme_id":"9974ae4d-42a5-4683-8086-e7f75a507fc8"} -> 201 {"id":"adcf5228-d352-4468-b5f1-93e30fa48ca2",...,"choice_window_snapshot":"ANY_TIME","superseded_at":null}

